A||||3||AkursedX||Cracked Manifold?||||5||
Z||000000||AkursedX||03-17-2001||12:19 PM||||Hello all,<P>Well I think I have a cracked exhaust manifold.  My evidence for it is that when I start up my car, I can see a little wisp of white smoke coming up near the dipstick on my '88GT.  It goes away after my car warms up, just like the with the regular exhaust.  <P>So do you guys think that this is my problem?  Or could it be something else?<P>Also, if it is the problem, about how much would it be to have them re-welded and ported, a general estimate?  <BR>And what about other options?  Does anyone have opinions on Chirs West's full length of shorty headers?  Or the sprint manifolds?  FOCOA headers?<P>I know I would have a loss of tourque, but I am in the process of saving up money for a build-up of my 2.8 for next winter, so I wouldn't mind paying the money for some high performance headers now.<P>All input is greatly apprecitaed.  Thank you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||KRMFiero||03-17-2001||01:30 PM||||well if it is your manifoild put your hand around and see if you can feel air coming out (i would only do this if the car was not warmed up so you dont get burned<P>also ckeak your EGR, it is possible that it is comming from there<P>kyle||||reg||1
Z||000002||Nashco||03-17-2001||05:47 PM||||An easier way to find exhaust leaks than feeling for them is listening for them.  If they're hard to locate, a really cool trick is to use a hose.  When I worked on cars, we'd always have heater hose laying around, which works great.  Any hose (garden hose is just as good) works for this, it just has to be about three or four feet long.  Plug one ear, put the hose to the other ear, and poke the other end of the hose all over around the exhaust and you'll be amazed at how well leaks can be defined.  You might even find some leaks that you didn't know you had before!<P>Hope this helps, have fun!<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||AkursedX||03-17-2001||06:12 PM||||Hello again, and thanks for the input.  I went out again today to see if i could confirm a leak.  I wasn't really able to find one, nor does it sound like i have one.<P>What i believe my problem is, is that the coolant tube that is near the oil dipstick and the manifold (v-6) might be leaking a little bit.  My car is in storage for the winter, so it doesn't get started all the time, so I think (hope), from sitting around, it's just dripping out a tiny bit of antifreeze that is getting burned off.||||reg||1
